# Seat: Product taste & emotional resonance — Round 7 (working notes)
# Build: commit 984a0f17, frozen. Written as-I-go.

## Confirmed by driving (running log)

1. **Dictation floor clock ticks** (0:00 -> 0:06). Not a defect. But the interim
   (grey) words never resolve to ink while the clock runs — the most cinematic
   screen in the suite is frozen except for the timer. Candidate.

2. **Timeline has no dock at any desk width.** `.dock` measures 370x48 in
   tasks.board and 348x46 in notes.notebook at both 1440 and 1920;
   timeline.owner-flight has NO .dock element with geometry at either width.
   Timeline's primary act ("Add a moment") is a top-right button instead.
   The locked architecture names "the dock at the foot" as part of the Studio
   Floor. Two of three products have it. CANDIDATE FINDING.

3. **The account tile renders TWICE** in Notes and Tasks (rail foot + dock),
   870-1100px apart, and the two copies do not carry the same accessible name:
     notes rail  "Orla, venue manager"
     notes dock  "Orla, venue manager. Not here yet."
     tasks rail  "Orla, venue manager"
     tasks dock  "Orla, venue manager"
     timeline rail "Orla, venue manager"  (no dock at all)
   CANDIDATE FINDING — check behaviour of each.

4. **The person is drawn twice at the foot.** CONFIRMED by crop
   (_zz-tst-foot.png, tasks.board @1440): `.railAvatar` OR (ghost, 32px, y=900)
   at bottom-left and `.dockAvatar` OR (FILLED INK, 34px, y=883) at x=907 —
   ~870px apart on the same eye-line. Both are `aria-disabled="true"`, both
   open the identical card "Not here yet." / title "Your account, in Signal
   Studio. Not here yet." So the shell shows the operator's monogram twice and
   both copies are the same dead door. Worse: the dock copy is filled ink,
   the same value as the "Add task" primary pill sitting 15px to its left —
   they read as one two-part control, so the second loudest object in the dock
   is a door that does not open. Timeline has neither dock nor a second copy,
   so the suite is also inconsistent about it.
   (Escape does correctly dismiss the card; the rail avatar IS reachable by
   ArrowDown on the roving rail. The honest-doors contract holds; the
   duplication and the ink weight are the defect.)

5. **HEADLINE — the arrival is a 2-pixel nudge.** MEASURED frame-by-frame
   (_zz-tst-arr2/3.mjs). Send -> "Open in Tasks" -> the card lands. The entire
   visual event on the arriving card is: `[data-settling]` toggled on, which
   animates transform from `translateY(-2px) scale(0.994)` to identity over
   ~420ms. Sampled every frame: opacity 1 throughout, background
   rgb(255,255,255) throughout, border-color rgb(17,17,17) throughout,
   box-shadow byte-identical throughout, no ::before/::after content, no class
   other than `card`. A 2px rise and a 1.5px width change on a 256px card.
   The card lands LAST in To do, looking exactly like the three cards above it.
   The gate proves a beat exists and is on the motion ladder; it cannot prove
   the beat READS, and this one does not. The one gesture that justifies a
   suite existing arrives without an event.

6. **HEADLINE #2 — the spine reassembles itself under your thumb on a phone.**
   MEASURED at 390x844 (touch), centre-x of the three product tiles in the
   capsule:
        in Notes     Notes@227  Tasks@271  Timeline@315   (pitch 44px, right)
        in Tasks     Notes@54   Tasks@130  Timeline@206   (pitch 76px, left)
        in Timeline  Notes@63   Tasks@157  Timeline@251   (pitch 94px, left)
   Tapping "Tasks" at x=271 while in Notes lands you in Tasks, where "Tasks"
   has moved to x=130 and x=271 is now bare capsule between More(243) and
   Add task(295). The Notes tile travels 173px — 44% of the screen — on every
   crossing, and the pitch changes three times. The architecture says one rail,
   rendered once, and on a phone the capsule and the dock are the same object.
   Measured, it is three objects.

7. **Two doors named "More" on one phone screen (Timeline @390).** Both
   visible simultaneously: capsule grid tile aria-label="More" 44x44 at
   (297,783), and a "···" aria-label="More" 39x44 at (160,140). One is the
   unbuilt honest door, the other opens the real Preview/link menu. Same word,
   two destinations, one 390px screen.
   And on the **Notes phone the "More" door has zero size** — `.railUtil`'s
   copy measures 0x0 at 390 and the Notes capsule carries no More tile, while
   Tasks (243,783) and Timeline (297,783) both keep theirs. The honest door
   that is supposed to be "present, reachable, in the tab order" is absent in
   one product at one width.
